Tool 3 — GitHub (Scenario-Based)
(DevOps Interview Real-Time Scenarios Questions)

These scenarios are exactly what happens in real DevOps & SRE teams 👇

GitHub – Scenario Based Interview Questions

1. A developer directly pushed to main. How will you prevent this in future?
2. A PR passed CI but broke production. What went wrong?
3. Secrets were leaked in a public repo. What immediate steps will you take?
4. How do you restrict deployments to production only after approvals?
5. A GitHub Actions workflow was modified by mistake. How do you recover it?
6. How do you stop untrusted PRs from accessing secrets?
7. Your GitHub Actions usage cost is very high. How will you reduce it?
8. CI pipelines are slow. How will you optimize them?
9. How do you isolate CI jobs for different environments?
10. How do you design multi-environment CI/CD in GitHub?
11. A self-hosted runner got compromised. What actions will you take?
12. How do you secure self-hosted runners?
13. How do you implement approval gates before deployment?
14. How do you restrict who can trigger workflows?
15. How do you integrate GitHub with AWS without static credentials?
16. How do you audit user actions in GitHub?
17. How do you enforce commit signing across org?
18. How do you handle monorepo CI pipelines?
19. How do you share artifacts across workflows?
20. How do you rollback a failed deployment using GitHub?
21. How do you protect release branches?
22. How do you restrict third-party GitHub Actions usage?
23. How do you detect malicious workflows?
24. How do you implement blue-green deployment with GitHub?
25. How do you prevent secrets exposure in forked repos?
26. How do you scale GitHub Actions for thousands of repos?
27. How do you manage GitHub org access at scale?
28. How do you comply with SOC2 using GitHub?
29. How do you rotate secrets without downtime?
30. How do you design GitHub as a secure enterprise CI/CD platform?
